Output: [<span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">=
3</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number"=
>0</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">0</span>]
</code></pre></div>
<h2 id=3D"intuition">Intuition</h2>
<p>This problem has three main requirements:</p>
<ol>
<li>Move all zeros to the end of the array.</li>
<li>Maintain the relative order of the non-zero elements.</li>
<li>Perform the modification in place.</li>
</ol>
<p>A naive approach to this problem is to build the output using a separate=
 array (<code>temp</code>). We can add all non-zero elements from the left =
of <code>nums</code> to this temporary array and leave the rest of it as ze=
ros. Then, we just set the input array equal to <code>temp</code>.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>By identifying and moving the non-zero elements from the left side of th=
e array first, we ensure their order is preserved when we add them to the o=
utput:</p>
</blockquote>
